repeat loop [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation executes the instruction within the repeat-loop one or more times. Plant Simulation
checks the condition after each loop iteration and only exits the loop when the condition is fulfilled. For
this reason the loop will always be executed at least once.
Remarks
If the condition never returns true, the loop will be executed infinitely. Press Ctrl+Alt+Shift to stop the
infinite loop and to open the Method-Debugger.
Example
var x: length
repeat
   x := methodEnterLength
until x >= 0
See also
Edit ribbon tab of the Method > Select Template > repeat-until
Exit a Loop with exitLoop
